    "body": "## What\nExtract build-only fork version preparation and reuse it from release:fork. Prepare public JS package identities before native/CLI builds without changing lockfiles, Cargo versions, dependency pins, changelogs, Git history, or PATH. Add a compiled runtime-version assertion to native CI.\n\nAlso correct the user-requested internal PR guidance in AGENTS.md, CONTRIBUTING.md, and the PR template: contributor-written sentences are required only for upstream submissions, not maintainer PRs in this fork.\n\n## Why\nThe clean upstream reconstruction retained fork-version derivation but reset source manifests to upstream versions. Arch builds bypassed release:fork and therefore reported upstream-only identity. The dependent Arch recipe will invoke preparation after frozen dependency installation and before compilation; it will land only after this source change passes CI and merges.\n\n## Testing\n- Full bun run check:ts passed (lint, formatting, workspace type checks).\n- Seven focused tests passed, including real Git-tag preparation and preservation of dependency/release inputs.\n- Executed preparation in a disposable real-source checkout: 18.4.2+vith-fork.307.8e4b0d21d444; utilities, native addon package and CLI manifests agree; Git HEAD and non-manifest inputs unchanged.\n- Arch recipe shell syntax passed. No local compilation or installed-binary replacement.\n- CI #53 passed lint, formatting, all workspace type checks, Rust check, web/native/CLI builds, and the exact compiled version assertion in 4m 49s. The built ARM executable was also run in its CI runtime image and printed omp/18.4.2+vith-fork.312.5712dbf40be4.\n- Per maintainer instruction, CI test execution (TS/Rust suites and worker smoke) is temporarily disabled until its runtime is optimized; lint, formatting/type checks and builds remain enabled. CI #50 was canceled, not passed.\n- Replaced the root-sensitive index-permission test fixture with a directory read failure; this regression test has not been rerun under the temporary no-tests policy.\n- Updated Woodpecker configuration passed strict validation with zero errors or warnings.\n- Changelog intentionally unchanged per fork policy; development documentation updated.\n\n---\n\n- [x] `bun check` passes\n- [x] Tested locally\n- [ ] CHANGELOG updated with the required attribution (if user-facing; internal issue fixes use issue links, external contributions add the PR link and contributor credit after creation)\n",
    "changed_files": 11,
