        "body": "## What\nInvoke the shared build-only fork preparation after frozen dependency installation and before compiling the native addon and executable. On an x86_64 build host, assert the compiled executable reports the prepared version.\n\n## Why\nArch pkgver already identifies the fork, but the executable still embeds upstream-only package manifests. Reuse the source-owned preparation instead of manually editing versions, .SRCINFO, or running release:fork inside makepkg.\n\n## Testing\n- bash -n passed.\n- Shared preparation and its real-source smoke are verified in source PR #5: https://git.n3t.work/vith/oh-my-pi/pulls/5.\n- No static PKGBUILD version or .SRCINFO changes.\n- Source PR #5 passed revised CI #53 (lint/format/type checks and shipping builds, tests disabled by maintainer instruction) and merged as eaeb9b7e6e8e6bfa10c73fa2f0c67122db4be6a4. Its built ARM executable reported the derived fork version.\n- Rechecked recipe shell syntax successfully. Package CI #144 succeeded and published the signed x86_64 package 18.4.2.vith.r313.geaeb9b7e6e8e-1. Installed through pacman with signature/integrity checks; PATH resolves to package-owned /usr/bin/omp, which reports omp/18.4.2+vith-fork.313.eaeb9b7e6e8e.\n",
